+ * On the RGMII trunk (SoC Port 0 <-> RTL8367S Port 6), full 1500B MTU IP
+ * frames carry BOTH the 4-byte 0x8899 Realtek CPU tag and the 4-byte 802.1Q
+ * VLAN tag simultaneously: 14 + 4 + 4 + 1500 + 4 = 1526 bytes. The RTL8367S
+ * power-on default CFG0 max length (0x088c) is 0x05f2 (1522 bytes), silently
+ * dropping full-MTU TCP segments (LuCI JS bundles, SSH KEXINIT) while passing
+ * small ICMP/HTTP headers. Program CFG0/CFG1 = 0x0610 (1552 bytes, matching
+ * SoC MACCR AcptMaxLen=1552) and select CFG0 in both rtl8367s_cpu_tag_enable()
+ * and rtl8367b_setup() so swconfig apply never clobbers 0x1200 back to 0x2000.
